# Automower® Connect API

This article is a guide for how you can control Automower® via code (Node.js in our case) with the help of the Husqvarna Automower® API.

## Authentication

Each request **MUST** be authenticated with all the following headers:

- `Authorization-Provider`: **MUST** contain value "husqvarna". Example:

Authorization-Provider: husqvarna

- `Authorization`: **MUST** contain string "Bearer " followed by the auth token obtained from Authentication API. Example:

Authorization: Bearer fc3c6ed9-eb35-4629-9652-d3272a600edc

- `X-Api-Key`: **MUST** contain the API key obtained from the developer portal. Example:

X-Api-Key: XST5MBDmoO37p3vJJKoaB5PAR4tc7TKX2u7kYrig


## Working with the API

Automower® Connect API consists of three resources on the endpoint [https://api.amc.husqvarna.dev/v1](https://api.amc.husqvarna.dev/v1).

### Get all my paired mowers

You use your Automower® Connect application (iOS/Android) to pair/unpair your mowers.

### Get a specific mower

Once you know which mower you want to control, this is the method to use. The model sent back from the Automower® Connect API is best described in the OPENAPI tab.

### Post an action to a specific mower

When you want to send commands to your mower this is the method to use. Please note that each command always contains an attribute named `type`. Depending on the `type` value you might also need to pass an `attributes` object. This is described in the OPENAPI tab.

When you do a `POST` action request and receive status `202` it does not mean that Automower® per default has started executing your command. This only means that our queue for mower commands has successfully processed your request and will as soon as possible send this command to the Automower®'s command queue. The advantage of this is that you get a really fast response while the drawback is that you will not know if the Automower® will execute your command instantly or in a moment.

**NOTE: If you send a `start` command, Automower® will not leave the charging station until it is fully charged.**

# Examples

The following examples assume you have an Application API Key and a valid `access_token`. Please refer to Authentication API for [documentation](https://developer.husqvarnagroup.cloud/apis/Authentication+API#/readme) about tokens.

You will need to have an Automower® Connect account with at least one connected Automower®. Please go to [Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.husqvarna.automowerconnect) or [Apple Store](https://itunes.apple.com/us/app/automower-connect/id983601778) to download the application.

